-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version], s 125B: the rate of tax on a dividend.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt (sha256 b87f2cf4...6b81b6).
--
-- WHAT IT SAYS. "Notwithstanding ss 121 and 126, the rate of tax on income from a dividend is:" (1) a dividend in the hands of an
-- individual, 25%; (2) notwithstanding (1), a dividend in the hands of an individual who was, at the time of receiving it or at some time
-- in the twelve months before, a material shareholder in the body of persons that paid it, 30%; (3) a dividend in the hands of a family
-- company, 25%, but 30% if the assessee as meant in s 64A was a material shareholder, directly or indirectly, in the paying company;
-- (4) a dividend not exempt in the hands of a public institution or a provident fund as defined in s 9(2), 25%; (5) a dividend in the
-- hands of a non-resident body of persons, 25%, but 30% if the body was, at the time of receipt or at some time in the twelve months
-- before, a material shareholder (s 88) in the payer.
--
-- WHICH DIVIDENDS IT ANSWERS. The deposited text is s 125B as amended at retrieval; its last amendment in the list at the head of the
-- section is the 5772 one (tag תשע״ב־2, 2012), and "the change date" of s 88 is 1 January 2012. A dividend received before the change
-- date is declined: the text of s 125B before the 2012 amendment is not deposited (NOTES.md, assumption A6; needs a source).
-- Section 125B(4) exempts nothing by itself: a dividend exempt in the hands of a public institution or provident fund has no rate here.
--
-- THE FORKS. S1 and S4 (inside s 88, "alone or together with another", and from which day the twelve months run) and D1: paragraph (3)
-- names no time at which the family company's shareholder is tested, where (2) and (5) name the twelve months. The default declines
-- where the readings give different answers; the rate is 25% or 30%, so any part of the readings that changes the status changes the answer.

§ `Section 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend`

-- src:4512 | סעיף 125ב – שיעור המס על דיבידנד [תיקון: תשל״ד־2, תשל״ה־2, תשמ״ז־2, תשמ״ז־4, תשמ״ז־5, תשנ״ב־7, תשנ״ו־3, תשס״ב־9, תשס״ה־4, תשס״ה־9, תשע״ב־2]
-- src:4513 | על אף האמור בסעיפים 121 ו־126, שיעור המס על הכנסה מדיבידנד יהיה כלהלן:
-- src:4514 | (1) דיבידנד בידי יחיד – 25%;
-- src:4515 | (2) על אף האמור בפסקה (1), דיבידנד בידי יחיד שהיה במועד קבלת הדיבידנד או במועד כלשהו בשנים עשר החודשים שקדמו לו, בעל מניות מהותי כהגדרתו בסעיף 88 בחבר־בני־אדם ששילם את הדיבידנד – 30%;
-- src:4516 | (3) דיבידנד בידי חברה משפחתית – 25%, ואולם אם היה הנישום כמשמעותו בסעיף 64א בעל מניות מהותי, במישרין או בעקיפין, בחברה ששילמה את הדיבידנד – 30%;
-- src:4517 | (4) דיבידנד שאינו פטור ממס בידי מוסד ציבורי או בידי קופת גמל כהגדרתם בסעיף 9(2) – 25%;
-- src:4518 | (5) דיבידנד בידי חבר־בני־אדם שהוא תושב חוץ – 25%, ואולם אם היה חבר־בני־האדם במועד קבלת הדיבידנד או במועד כלשהו ב־12 החודשים שקדמו לו בעל מניות מהותי כהגדרתו בסעיף 88 – 30%.

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 125B as deposited states the rates for a dividend from the change date on` MEANS
    REFUSE "the deposited text of section 125B is the text as amended in 2012, and the text before it is not deposited"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 125B has no paragraph for this recipient` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 125B has no paragraph for this recipient"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 125B(4) sets a rate only for a dividend that is not exempt in the hands of the recipient` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 125B(4) sets a rate only for a dividend that is not exempt in the hands of the recipient"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`whether the recipient was a material shareholder depends on a reading section 88 leaves open, and here the rate turns on it` MEANS
    REFUSE "whether the recipient was a material shareholder depends on a reading section 88 leaves open, and here the rate turns on it"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 125B(3) names no time at which the shareholding is tested, and here the rate turns on it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 125B(3) names no time at which the shareholding is tested, and here the rate turns on it"

-- 25% unless material shareholder, in which case 30%: a status settled as a MAYBE.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 125B(1)-(2), (5) (source lines 4514-4515, 4518)
GIVEN `the status` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 125B — 25%, or 30% for a material shareholder, the status being` `the status` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN JUST isMaterial THEN IF isMaterial THEN 30% ELSE 25%
    WHEN NOTHING         THEN `whether the recipient was a material shareholder depends on a reading section 88 leaves open, and here the rate turns on it`

-- Paragraph (3): the status of the person meant in s 64A, tested at the time fork D1 names: at receipt only, at receipt or in the twelve months before, or (0.1.1) at any time up to receipt;
-- the first days of each reading are listed together and the answer is given if every one of them gives the same.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 125B(3) (source line 4516); fork D1
GIVEN `the day`     IS A DATE
      `the records` IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
      r             IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 125B(3) — whether the person meant in section 64A is a material shareholder, on` `the day` `by the records` `the records` `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    `s 88 — whether a material shareholder on a recorded day from any of` `the first days` `up to` `the day` `, by the records` `the records` `, reading together with another as` (r's `together with another`)
    WHERE
        `the first days` MEANS
            CONSIDER r's `the time of the test in section 125B(3)`
            WHEN `at the time of receiving the dividend only`                                     THEN `receipt only`
            WHEN `at the time of receiving the dividend or at some time in the twelve months before it` THEN `twelve months`
            WHEN `at any time up to the receiving of the dividend`                                 THEN `any time`
            WHEN `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`                           THEN append `receipt only` (append `twelve months` `any time`)
        `receipt only` MEANS LIST `the day`
        `twelve months` MEANS `s 88 — the candidate first days of the twelve months before` `the day` `, reading them as` (r's `the twelve months before a day`)
        `any time` MEANS LIST (YMD 1900 1 1)

-- The rate for a dividend received on a day by a recipient of one of the kinds.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 125B(1)-(5) (source lines 4514-4518); forks S1, S4, D1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the day`       IS A DATE
      `the recipient` IS A `The recipient of a dividend, for section 125B`
      r               IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day` `by` `the recipient` `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    IF   `the day` LESS THAN `s 88 — the change date`
    THEN `section 125B as deposited states the rates for a dividend from the change date on`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the recipient`
         WHEN `an individual` `the records`
           THEN `s 125B — 25%, or 30% for a material shareholder, the status being` (`s 88 — whether a material shareholder on` `the day` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` `the records` `, reading the forks as` r)
         WHEN `a family company` `the records`
           THEN CONSIDER `s 125B(3) — whether the person meant in section 64A is a material shareholder, on` `the day` `by the records` `the records` `, reading the forks as` r
                WHEN JUST isMaterial THEN IF isMaterial THEN 30% ELSE 25%
                WHEN NOTHING         THEN `section 125B(3) names no time at which the shareholding is tested, and here the rate turns on it`
         WHEN `a public institution or a provident fund as defined in section 9(2)` `exempt`
           THEN IF `exempt` THEN `section 125B(4) sets a rate only for a dividend that is not exempt in the hands of the recipient` ELSE 25%
         WHEN `a non-resident body of persons` `the records`
           THEN `s 125B — 25%, or 30% for a material shareholder, the status being` (`s 88 — whether a material shareholder on` `the day` `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` `the records` `, reading the forks as` r)
         WHEN `any other recipient`
           THEN `section 125B has no paragraph for this recipient`

-- The tax: the rate times the dividend.
GIVEN `the dividend` IS A NUMBER
      `the day`       IS A DATE
      `the recipient` IS A `The recipient of a dividend, for section 125B`
      r               IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 125B — the tax on a dividend of` `the dividend` `received on` `the day` `by` `the recipient` `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    `the dividend` TIMES `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day` `by` `the recipient` `, reading the forks as` r
